 of  information one for the msa  representation on top and another flow  of information  for the pair representation at the  bottom all these 48  blocks have individual parameters so  this is not a recurrent network unlike  the structure module that we'll discuss  in a bit  each block has an msa and a pair  representation as  input as well as its output and it  processes them with several layers  now the layers inside the evil former  well they actually have a lot of  very clever technical tricks that make  it particularly  suitable for updating the protein  representations coming from the input  stage  and the main idea here is to allow the  network to iteratively refine the  information  from the msa and pair representations by  allowing the two modalities to exchange  information  which essentially enables direct  reasoning  about the spatial and the evolutionary  relationships  in the protein so to translate this in  plain english the idea  is that the multiple sequence alignment  contains information about the  evolutionary trajectory  of mutations for the particular protein  in question  but in order to extract all the relevant  information from this msa  well you would have to know something  about the structure that you're dealing  with  and this is what the pair representation  tries to do so in essence these two  flows of information  are just interacting together to solve  an evolutionary puzzle  about the input protein now i'm not  going to go into all the technical  details of how exactly the evil former  does this since there's just  way too much stuff and you really need  to read the supplementary to the paper  if you want to dive deep in the rabbit  hole  but very briefly the msa stack uses an  attention schema called  actual attention whereby alternating  layers  apply row and column attention  sequentially  the idea being that the row wise  attention  allows the model to reason about  information  from each of the aligned sequence  separately while the column attention  lets the model reason about  relationships between the aligned  residues  in different sequences of the msa stack  additionally the row attention is  influenced by a branch coming from the  bottom  allowing the information from the pair  representations to flow  into the msa stack likewise another  branch of the network goes back down to  the bottom flow  to enable an update of the pair  representations  now interestingly this operation is  applied within  every one of the 48 blocks in the evil  former  enabling continuous communication  between the evolving  msa and pair representations now the  pair representations themselves  are updated using another very specific  mechanism  that essentially tries to make the 2d  representations  consistent with the three-dimensional  structure that they represent  and to understand what's happening here  consider that the purpose of these 2d  representations  is to encode things like inter-residue  distances  but there's a bit of a problem here  remember that the feature vector at  position i  j should encode the distance between  residues i  and j so now imagine creating a triangle  in 3d space  going from i to j the k now because  these  two-dimensional features are the output  of the neural net  well it's very likely that the predicted  distances in the 2d feature map  are actually incompatible with any  possible physical triangle  in 3d space and this is why this part of  the network  allows the 2d feature map to update  itself  in such a way that it becomes more  consistent  with an actual three-dimensional  structure again  if you want to learn how exactly alpha  fold does this you should definitely  check out the paper because there's some  very clever tricks  here but so that's the general idea  behind the evil former to gradually  mix information between the msa and the  pair representations  to prepare for structure generation in  the structure module  so the final piece of alpha fold is the  