sult  of a single breakthrough idea that  magically solves the protein folding  problem  instead it's a collection of cleverly  designed  and novel ideas that have been improved  over many design cycles  resulting in this amazingly well  engineered system  and there you go that's alpha fall 2 in  all its glory  so to end this video let's briefly zoom  out a little bit and talk about the  bigger picture  i mean is protein folding really solved  now  well yes and no first of all  let me state this very clearly alpha  fold is a tremendous engineering  achievement by some of the most talented  ai researchers in the world  the model is able to predict the  structures of most  single domain proteins in biology with  incredible accuracy  and it's undeniable that this will  herald a completely new era in  computational biology  where ai will be used as an  indispensable tool  for designing new drugs understanding  disease pathways  fighting viruses and much more at the  same time however alpha folds accuracy  isn't always perfect for example many  processes in biology rely on  large protein complexes whereby many  different proteins come together  to form complex molecular machines which  are currently  outside of alpha volt's capabilities  there's also the notion of  generalization i mean  alpha fold was trained on a data set of  proteins that naturally occur in biology  but we don't really know how good its  predictions will generalize  to completely new de novo proteins that  we might want to design with these new  tools  additionally most proteins function by  changing  shape with respect to targets they bind  to and  these molecular dynamics well they're  not captured by  alpha fold's static view of protein  structure  being able to model the flexibility of a  real protein in these different  conformations  will be crucial to study protein protein  interactions  that being said though it's very likely  that the ideas proposed by the alpha  fall team  can be extended to